                <pb facs="0591" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg581"/>

                <head>Appendix 280</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram From Budapest to
                        Communication</hi>[<hi rendition="#italic">s</hi>] <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Section, Supreme Economic Council, Paris</hi></p>
                <p>The opening of Danube has caused great activity in shipping circles. New Danubian
                    states and British shipping companies engaged in negotiations for transfer of
                    shipping from former owners are unable to complete transactions and commence
                    operations owing to doubtful title of ships in river. It is imperative for
                    welfare of all Danubian countries and river navigation that the American
                    Arbitrator referred to in treaty should commence his arbitrage with the least
                    possible delay. No. 44.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiral Troubridge</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Budapest</hi><lb/>103pm</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
